":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.3871","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,5]],"date-time":"2026-05-05T13:53:18Z","timestamp":1777989198162,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"PeerJ","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.3772\/table-3","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,17]],"date-time":"2026-04-17T08:15:22Z","timestamp":1776413722000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Table 3: Extended binary metrics on IMDb and Amazon dataset."],"prefix":"10.7717","member":"4443","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,17]],"date-time":"2026-04-17T08:15:23Z","timestamp":1776413723000},"score":30.751196,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/peerj.com\/articles\/cs-3772\/table-3"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7717\/peerj-cs.3772\/table-3","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.3772","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T09:31:43Z","timestamp":1772271103375,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"PeerJ","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.2011\/supp-1","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,4,30]],"date-time":"2024-04-30T04:34:13Z","timestamp":1714451653000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Supplemental Information 1: The YELP-5 dataset is a sentiment classification task dataset used for sentiment analysis. It comprises user reviews sourced from the Yelp website"],"prefix":"10.7717","member":"4443","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,4,30]],"date-time":"2024-04-30T04:34:19Z","timestamp":1714451659000},"score":30.720398,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/peerj.com\/articles\/cs-2011\/supp-1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7717\/peerj-cs.2011\/supp-1","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.7717\/peerj-cs.2011","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,13]],"date-time":"2026-04-13T11:05:02Z","timestamp":1776078302535,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"EWA Publishing","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ACE"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Sentiment analysis has become crucial for understanding consumer behavior in e-commerce and social media. While models based on transformers like Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers (BERT) and A Robustly Optimized BERT Pretraining Approach (RoBERTa) have great performance in Natural Language Processing (NLP) tasks, challenges persist in domain-specific language nuances and context sensitivity. This study addresses these gaps by utilizing DeBERTa, an advanced model with disentangled attention mechanisms, to improve sentiment classification. The methodology involves fine-tuning the DeBERTa-base on the IMDb dataset and evaluating its generalization on the Amazon Polarity dataset. The results achieved 93.21% accuracy, 91.28% precision, 94.98% recall, and 93.32% F1 score, achieving a good balance between precision and recall while maintaining high accuracy. The result of this study demonstrates that Decoding-enhanced BERT with Disentangled Attention (DeBERTa) has strong performance in handling long, structured text and short, diverse comments. This illustrates DeBERTa's superiority in capturing complex semantic relationships and context-dependent sentiments.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.54254\/2755-2721\/2025.kl22625","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]],"date-time":"2025-05-06T05:23:23Z","timestamp":1746509003000},"page":"198-201","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Enhancing Sentiment Analysis with Fine-Tuned DeBERTa in a Cross-Domain Study on IMDb and Amazon Polarity Datasets"],"prefix":"10.54254","volume":"149","author":[{"given":"Zijian","family":"Cao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Dundee International Institute, Central South University, Changsha, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"32523","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]]},"container-title":["Applied and Computational Engineering"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,13]],"date-time":"2026-04-13T10:15:11Z","timestamp":1776075311000},"score":30.442432,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ace.ewapub.com\/article\/view\/22625"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,22]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.54254\/2755-2721\/2025.kl22625","ISSN":["2755-2721","2755-273X"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2755-2721","type":"print"},{"value":"2755-273X","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,6]]}},{"institution":[{"name":"Front Matter"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,28]],"date-time":"2026-02-28T07:42:09Z","timestamp":1772264529734,"version":"3.50.1"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2008,9,3]]},"group-title":"iRights.info","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Front Matter","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2008,9,3]],"date-time":"2008-09-03T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1220400000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/legalcode"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2008,9,3]],"date-time":"2008-09-03T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1220400000000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/legalcode"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Wer schon immer an der Biographie\/Diskographie seiner Lieblingsmusiker und -innen herumbasteln wollte, darf sich ab sofort bei SoundUnwound, einer Art Musiker-Wiki von IMDb und Amazon austoben. Vorerst gibt es SoundUnwound nur in englischer Sprache; ob nach dem Vorbild von Wikipedia andere Sprachen folgen werden, ist derzeit nicht bekannt.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.59350\/fn0ff-ysa09","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,4]],"date-time":"2023-12-04T18:53:05Z","timestamp":1701715985000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Musiker-Wiki von IMDb und Amazon"],"prefix":"10.59350","author":[{"given":"Robert A.","family":"Gehring","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"31795","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/irights.info\/2008\/09\/03\/musiker-wiki-von-imdb-und-amazon\/308","content-type":"text\/html","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.rogue-scholar.org\/posts\/10.59350\/fn0ff-ysa09.md","content-type":"text\/plain","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.rogue-scholar.org\/posts\/10.59350\/fn0ff-ysa09.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.rogue-scholar.org\/posts\/10.59350\/fn0ff-ysa09.epub","content-type":"application\/epub+zip","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.rogue-scholar.org\/posts\/10.59350\/fn0ff-ysa09.xml","content-type":"application\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,5]],"date-time":"2025-12-05T18:30:07Z","timestamp":1764959407000},"score":29.82806,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/irights.info\/2008\/09\/03\/musiker-wiki-von-imdb-und-amazon\/308"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2008,9,3]]},"references-count":0,"version":{"version":"v1"},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.59350\/fn0ff-ysa09","relation":{"is-version-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.59350\/0d5gq-x9q81","asserted-by":"object"}]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2008,9,3]]},"subtype":"other"},{"institution":[{"name":"Front Matter"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,5]],"date-time":"2025-12-05T18:33:45Z","timestamp":1764959625584,"ver